# {{ project.name }}

A full-stack TypeScript web app: a [Fastify](https://fastify.dev) API and a [Vue 3](https://vuejs.org) single-page app, sharing one SQLite database.

## Requirements

{%- if choices.docker == "full" %}
- Docker 24 or newer with Docker Compose. Everything runs in containers; Node.js is not needed on this machine.
{%- else %}
- Node.js 24 or newer, npm 10 or newer
{%- if choices.docker == "run" %}
- Docker 24 or newer with Docker Compose (only for running in a container)
{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}

## Quick start

```sh
[ -f .env ] || cp .env.example .env   # first run after cloning
{%- if choices.docker == "full" %}
docker compose run --rm dev npm install
docker compose up dev
{%- else %}
npm install
npm run dev
{%- endif %}
```

Open http://localhost:{{ ports.WEB_PORT }}. The API listens on http://localhost:{{ ports.APP_PORT }}; the Vite dev server proxies `/api` to it.

Production-style run on a single port:

```sh
{%- if choices.docker == "full" %}
docker compose up --build app   # API + built web app on http://localhost:{{ ports.APP_PORT }}
{%- else %}
npm run build
npm start                  # API + built web app on http://localhost:{{ ports.APP_PORT }}
{%- endif %}
```

## Scripts
{% if choices.docker == "full" %}
Run them in the dev container: `docker compose run --rm dev npm run <script>` (`npm run dev` → `docker compose up dev`).
{% endif %}
| Command                             | What it does                                                               |
| ----------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `npm run dev`                       | API (restarts on file changes) and Vite dev server (hot reload) together   |
| `npm run build`                     | Type-check everything and build the web app into `web/dist`                |
| `npm start`                         | Serve the API and the built web app on `APP_PORT`                          |
| `npm test`                          | Run all tests (Vitest: server and web)                                     |
| `npm run check`                     | Lint, format check, type-check, tests, security check: the quality gate    |
| `npm run walls`                     | `walls check` (needs `walls`: `npm link` in `~/Documents/walls`)           |
| `npm run security`                  | `secbase check` (needs `secbase`: `npm link` in `~/Documents/secbase`)     |
| `npm run lint` / `npm run lint:fix` | ESLint                                                                     |
| `npm run format`                    | Format all files with Prettier                                             |
| `npm run typecheck`                 | `vue-tsc --build` for the server, the web app and the scripts              |
| `npm run db:migrate`                | Apply pending database migrations (also done on server start)              |

## Configuration

All settings live in `.env` in the project root. It is git-ignored; `.env.example` documents every key and is committed. The server reads `.env` at startup, Vite reads it at dev/build time and exposes only `APP_NAME` to the browser.

| Key | Value | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `APP_NAME` | `{{ env.APP_NAME }}` | App name shown in the UI and returned by `GET /api/health` |
| `APP_SLUG` | `{{ env.APP_SLUG }}` | Machine-friendly name |
| `APP_HOST` | `127.0.0.1` | Interface the API binds to; loopback only (Docker Compose sets `0.0.0.0` inside containers) |
| `APP_PORT` | `{{ ports.APP_PORT }}` | API port (`npm start` also serves the web app here) |
| `PUBLIC_URL` | _(empty)_ | Public URL once published; an `https://` URL turns on HSTS; its host is accepted in `Host` |
| `ALLOWED_HOSTS` | _(empty)_ | More host names the app answers to (comma-separated); other `Host` headers get 421 |
| `MAX_BODY_BYTES` | `1048576` | Largest accepted request body (1 MiB) |
| `WEB_PORT` | `{{ ports.WEB_PORT }}` | Vite dev server port |
| `DB_PATH` | `{{ env.DB_PATH }}` | SQLite file, relative to the project root |
| `LOG_LEVEL` | `info` | `fatal`, `error`, `warn`, `info`, `debug`, `trace` or `silent` |
{%- if choices.docker != "none" %}
| `COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME` | `{{ project.slug }}` | Docker Compose project name |
| `DOCKER_DATA` | `{{ env.DOCKER_DATA }}` | Where containers keep the database: `data` (Docker volume) or `./data` (project folder) |
{%- endif %}

## Project structure

```text
server/   Fastify API (TypeScript run directly by Node), SQLite migrations, tests
web/      Vue 3 + Vite single-page app, Pinia stores, Tailwind CSS, tests
scripts/  Development helpers (npm run dev)
data/     SQLite database files (git-ignored)
```

The example feature **Notes** shows every layer end to end: SQL migration → repository → service → route → API client → Pinia store → page.
