## Docker
{% if choices.docker == "full" %}
Everything runs in containers. The `dev` service mounts this folder and keeps dependencies in Docker volumes:

```sh
docker compose run --rm dev npm install      # after cloning or changing dependencies
docker compose up dev                        # development with hot reload
docker compose run --rm dev npm run check    # any npm script
docker compose up --build app                # production container on http://localhost:{{ ports.APP_PORT }}
docker compose build app                     # only build the production image
docker compose --profile dev down            # stop everything; add -v to also delete the volumes
```
{% else %}
```sh
docker compose up --build   # build the image and run the app on http://localhost:{{ ports.APP_PORT }}
docker compose logs -f      # follow the logs
docker compose down         # stop; add -v to also delete the database volume
docker compose build app    # only build the production image
```
{% endif %}
The image builds the web app, keeps only the server's production dependencies and runs `node server/src/index.ts`, serving the API and the UI on `APP_PORT`. Compose reads `.env`: `COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME` names the stack and `APP_NAME` is passed to the web build. The SQLite database is stored {% if choices.data == "local" %}in the project's `data/` folder (`DOCKER_DATA=./data`){% else %}in the Docker volume `data` (`DOCKER_DATA=data`){% endif %}; change `DOCKER_DATA` in `.env` to switch.
{% endif %}
